<title>CANADA: TABLE - Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended July 2, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					Wk to Jy 2  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  28.78   +0.605    +1.085</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     1.82   -4.696    -4.614</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	456.73   -5.082    -8.658</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 120.40   -1.200   -38.100</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.30   -0.034    +1.961</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   May 97     Apr 97     May 96</p>
<p>M1					  71.01	69.62	61.02</p>
<p>M2					 391.85     390.50     391.67</p>
<p>M3					 505.70     502.76     481.50</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			May	   April</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-14.59	-17.30</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     714.38	708.03</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    102.60	105.66</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
